[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-32", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 32 — the update stream replayed in simulation time with the dependency rule; 2130 / 3372 ops/s", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-32.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 32 - the update stream replayed in simulation time, with the dependency rule\n\n> Seed: iteration 31's S22 - the certified driver's shape. Judge:\n> bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung SF1 subset; SUT levi, driver judah over\n> the LAN; impl :datalog.\n\n## Generate\n\n  Until now inserts were a fixed share of the read mix. The LDBC driver\n  does something else: every stream event carries a simulation time and\n  a dependency time; it is scheduled at t0 + (sim - sim0) * TCR and may\n  not start until every event with a smaller simulation time has\n  completed. The driver gained --tcr, read-stream (every event of the\n  forum and person streams, unsupported types keep :params nil), a\n  second queue, and a sorted-set of in-flight simulation times; reads\n  fill the slots while an event waits on its dependency.\n\n  Stream density measured first: 0.22 events per simulation-second, so\n  TCR 0.0002 s per sim-ms asks ~1,100 events/s, of which ~half are\n  INS4/INS5 (forums, memberships) this SUT does not hold - skipped,\n  counted beside completed, never an operation or a failure.\n\n  Prediction, written first: 8 slots at reads 1024/s + TCR 0.0002\n  passes; 32 slots at reads 2048/s + TCR 0.0001 (twice the density)\n  fails the 95% rule.\n\n## Rank\n\n    slots  reads/s  tcr      upd sent/s  on-time%  thru/s   verdict\n      8     1536    0.0002      595       100.00   2130.2   pass\n     32     2560    0.00015     813       100.00   3371.6   pass\n     32     2048    0.0001     ~1100       87.46   4124.3   FAILS (delay p95 2315 ms) - control\n\n  Both predictions held. Read-after-write over the interleave: 184\n  checked / 0 not visible / 10-16 outside a full IC07 window / 50-56\n  unverifiable, on each sweep. SUT heap 792 MB after gc, rss 2158 MB,\n  swap 24% - resident; /ldbc/meta now runs System/gc before reporting\n  used heap so the residency rule (rss >= 0.95 x used heap) is judged\n  on live data, not on garbage macOS has compressed.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - The stream is not free: at 32 slots the read-only 11-op column was\n    4089/s (iteration 29); with the stream at TCR 0.00015 the passing\n    point is 2560 reads + 813 updates = 3371.6. The dependency rule is\n    what costs - an event waiting on a smaller sim time holds a slot's\n    worth of scheduling even while reads use the slot.\n  - The first measurement counted skipped events as throughput (2114.9\n    at 8 slots). Corrected before recording: skipped events are not\n    operations. The honest 8-slot row is 2130.2 at a higher read rate.\n  - This is the certified driver's control loop in shape; what is still\n    missing for M2 is INS4/INS5 (so nothing is skipped), IS6, and the\n    ACID suite. TCR is now a first-class knob and the SUT's\n    :updates-applied is a rate (813/s at the passing 32-slot point).\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: GROWTH by shape (the interleave\nis the benchmark's, and the rule discriminated a failing point) with a\nlower 32-slot number than iteration 31's fixed-share row - reported as\nsuch, not hidden. Ratio to the audited No.1: 65 at 8 slots, 41 at 32.\n\nSeeds for iteration 33, in order:\n\n  - S23 (INS4/INS5 + IS6): forums and memberships, so the stream is\n    replayed whole and nothing is skipped.\n  - On decision: ADR-2609121100 (singleton counterparts), then SF1\n    proper on levi with the whole mix under the interleave.\n  - S15: static tables for the remaining IC operations.\n"}]
